s on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Susie Lee (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Susie Lee, the Democratic incumbent, seeks reelection in a Las Vegas-area district that has been among the closest in the country, with both of her general elections decided by fewer than four points. She enters the fall with a financial edge, having raised about $4.4 million to Martin O'Donnell's $4.1 million, and with most nonpartisan raters placing the race in the Likely Democratic column, though a few call it Lean Democratic.\n\nPrediction markets give Lee roughly a 95 percent chance of holding the seat. O'Donnell, a first-time candidate, has faced questions about his residency and criticism of an early television ad, while Republicans hope the no-tax-on-tips policy resonates in a service-economy district. A low-funded independent is also on the ballot. With no public general-election polls available, the outlook rests on ratings, money, and district fundamentals, which favor Lee by a solid but not overwhelming margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9366, "margin": 9.91}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9036, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9329, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9282, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9091, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.906, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9242, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.942, "margin": 10.2}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.921, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9325, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.93, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9287, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.8974, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.905, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9112, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.8961, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9316, "margin": 10.0}, {"dat